From bc7932ab56a99f71529630b22d7dadb7e67c14d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:26:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] raidz: fix born/free boundary of raidz_expansion_accounting

Follow-up fixes for "raidz: fix space accounting after expansion".

- Use the txg after activation as the per-birth-txg boundary, and
  persist it in the MOS (org.openzfs:raidz_expansion_accounting_txg)
  instead of deriving it from enabled_txg.  Sync tasks run after dirty
  datasets are synced, so blocks born in the activating txg were
  charged at the legacy ratio and must be freed at it.  enabled_txg is
  also wrong when an expansion completed between enablement and
  activation (e.g. on software without this feature).  The feature no
  longer depends on enabled_txg.
- Always (re)assign spa_raidz_expand_acct_txg on load and clear it in
  spa_unload(), so spa_load_retry() rewinds cannot keep a stale value.
- Recompute vdev_deflate_ratio_current when a reflow completes, so the
  capacity correction applies without re-importing the pool.
- Exclude the embedded log metaslab's free space from the correction,
  read vdev stats under vdev_stat_lock, and share one helper between
  spa_update_dspace() and spa_prop_get_config().
- Skip the vd_expand_lock lookup in vdev_get_deflate_ratio() for
  non-RAIDZ vdevs.
- zpool-features.7: the feature is read-only compatible, and activates
  immediately when enabled on an already-expanded pool.
- Add raidz_expand_013_pos for blocks born in the enabling txg.

Not addressed: once the feature is active, spa_update_dspace() still
values post-boundary allocations at the legacy ratio, so available
space is understated; see the XXX comment in spa_update_dspace().

